# Cloudflare Pages response headers.
#
# Vite copies public/ into dist/ verbatim, so this ships as dist/_headers.
# The COOP/COEP pair in vite.config.js applies to the dev server only — Vite
# does not put them in the build — so without this file a deployed copy is
# quietly slower than a local one.

# Cross-origin isolation, which is what enables SharedArrayBuffer and therefore
# multi-threaded WASM in onnxruntime. This is a performance floor, not a
# requirement: the Kokoro worker tries WebGPU first and never needs it, and
# browsers without WebGPU fall back to single-threaded inference if these are
# missing — noticeably slower, but working.
#
# `credentialless` rather than the `require-corp` used in dev, because the model
# weights stream from huggingface.co at runtime. Both modes can work — HF does
# send CORS headers — but require-corp is the strict one about cross-origin
# subresources, and credentialless removes that failure mode for no cost.
/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: credentialless
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin

# Everything Vite emits here is content-hashed, so it can never go stale.
# Worth being explicit given the ONNX runtime alone is 21 MB — a returning
# family member should pay that once, not once per visit.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
